Based on the search results, here's what I found about the OpenRouter Gemini 2.5 Flash Image generation API documentation:

## Model Overview

Gemini 2.5 Flash Image (also called "Nano Banana") is a state-of-the-art image generation model with contextual understanding, capable of image generation, edits, and multi-turn conversations.

## API Endpoint

To generate images, send a request to the /api/v1/chat/completions endpoint with the modalities parameter.

## Modalities Parameter

For Gemini models that output both text and images, use modalities: ["image", "text"].

## Image Configuration

Some image generation models support additional configuration through the image_config parameter, which can be used to set image_config.aspect_ratio to request specific aspect ratios for generated images. You can also set image_config.image_size to control the resolution of generated images.

## Key Documentation Resources

The main OpenRouter documentation for image generation can be found at:
- **Image Generation Guide**: https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/image-generation
- **Gemini 2.5 Flash Image API**: https://openrouter.ai/google/gemini-2.5-flash-image/api

These resources provide sample code and complete API specifications for implementing image generation with this model.


