Based on the search results, here's what I found about Gemini API image generation and text-to-image modalities in 2026:

## Current Image Generation Capabilities

Gemini models can generate and edit images using both text-only and text-and-image prompts. The API supports this through a multimodal approach.

## Available Models for Image Generation

Gemini 2.5 Flash Image and Gemini 3 Pro Image preview support generating images of people with updated safety filters. Gemini 2.5 Flash Image can generate images in 1024px, while Gemini 3 Pro Image can generate images up to 4096px.

## Response Modalities

You must include responseModalities: ["TEXT", "IMAGE"] in your configuration. Image-only output is not supported with these models. You can ask a Gemini model to generate and edit images using both text-only and text-and-image prompts.

## Model Retirement Notice

It's worth noting that Gemini 2.0 Flash and Gemini 2.0 Flash-Lite models will be retired on March 31, 2026, so developers should update to a newer model like gemini-2.5-flash-lite to avoid service disruption.

The Gemini API provides flexible text-to-image generation capabilities with support for various aspect ratios, resolutions, and interleaved text-and-image outputs for creating complex multimodal content.


