    "sender": "team-lead",
    "target": "@team-lead",
    "summary": "Gemini 2.5 Flash Image research complete",
    "content": "## Research Findings: Gemini 2.5 Flash Image Best Practices for Fashion Applications (2026)\n\n### Executive Summary\n\nGemini 2.5 Flash Image (aka \"Nano Banana\") is Google's state-of-the-art natively multimodal image generation model, now generally available as of February 2026. It excels at text-to-image, image editing, multi-image composition, and character consistency - making it well-suited for fashion photography and virtual try-on applications.\n\n---\n\n## 1. Native Image Generation Capabilities\n\n### Core Modalities\n- **Input**: Text, images (up to 5 reference images for character consistency)\n- **Output**: MUST specify `responseModalities: [\"TEXT\", \"IMAGE\"]` - image-only output is NOT supported\n- **Architecture**: Natively multimodal, trained from ground up to process text and images in unified step\n\n### Key Capabilities\n- **Text-to-image**: Generate high-quality images from text descriptions\n- **Image + text editing**: Upload photos and modify elements, change style, adjust colors\n- **Multi-image fusion**: Combine up to 5 images into single seamless composition\n- **Iterative refinement**: Conversational editing over multiple turns\n- **Character consistency**: Preserve faces, hairstyles, outfits across scenes\n- **Text rendering**: Generate clear text in images (logos, diagrams, posters)\n\n### Technical Specifications\n- **Resolution**: 1024px standard (Gemini 2.5 Flash Image), up to 4096px (Gemini 3 Pro Image)\n- **Aspect Ratios**: 10 supported ratios (1:1, 2:3, 3:2, 3:4, 4:3, 4:5, 5:4, 9:16, 16:9, 21:9)\n- **Pricing**: $30/1M output tokens, each image = 1290 tokens (~$0.039/image)\n- **Rate Limits**: 500 RPM for Tier 1 users (preview status)\n\n---\n\n## 2. Content Policy & Avoiding Rejections\n\n### Known Issues\nGoogle acknowledged that Gemini's filters \"became way more cautious than we intended,\" causing rejections even for innocuous prompts like \"a dog\" or \"a bowl of cereal.\"\n\n### Best Practices for Fashion/Clothing\n\n#### Be Hyper-Specific\n- **Always declare art style explicitly**: \"realistic photography\", \"digital art\", \"illustration\"\n- **Add specific details**: materials, colors, textures, locations, lighting\n- **Example**: Instead of \"dress\", use \"blue floral midi dress with puff sleeves, cotton fabric, natural lighting\"\n\n#### Include Context and Intent\n- Explain the purpose: \"Create a product photo for e-commerce\", \"fashion editorial for lookbook\"\n- Add scene context: \"flat-lay product photo\", \"studio photography\", \"outdoor lifestyle shot\"\n\n#### For Human Figures\n- Use \"fictional character\" or \"model\" language explicitly\n- Avoid ambiguous human descriptions\n- Be clear about clothing being on a person vs. flat-lay\n\n#### Safety Configuration\n- Gemini API provides configurable safety thresholds across 4 harm categories\n- Adjust to appropriate levels for fashion/commercial use\n\n#### Key Safety Tip\nContext matters - Google considers educational, documentary, artistic, or scientific applications when evaluating outputs. Frame your prompts with clear commercial/artistic intent.\n\n---\n\n## 3. Prompt Engineering for Fashion Photography\n\n### Flat-Lay Fashion Photography\n\n#### Template\n```\nA high-resolution, studio-lit flat-lay photograph of [product description] arranged on [surface type]. The layout is [composition style]. Photographed from directly overhead with [lighting setup] to create [lighting effect]. Shot with [camera/lens details]. [Aspect ratio].\n```\n\n#### Best Practices\n- Mention \"top-down\" or \"overhead\" perspective explicitly\n- Describe surface material (marble, concrete, wood, white seamless)\n- Specify product arrangement (centered, artful composition, with accessories)\n- Use photographic language: \"three-point softbox\", \"diffused natural light\", \"sharp focus\"\n\n#### Example Prompt\n```\nA high-resolution, studio-lit flat-lay photograph of a minimalist black leather handbag with gold hardware, positioned on polished white marble. The bag is centered with complementary items: sunglasses, a watch, and scattered white rose petals. Photographed from directly overhead with soft, diffused lighting to eliminate harsh shadows. Shot with a 50mm lens for natural perspective. Square 1:1 format.\n```\n\n### Virtual Try-On / Model Generation\n\n#### Character Consistency Features\n- Upload up to 5 reference images to maintain face/character consistency\n- Model preserves facial features, hairstyles, distinctive appearance across scenes\n- Each regeneration is NEW output - identity is NOT locked (unlike some face-consistency tools)\n\n#### Best Practices for Preserving Faces\n1. **Strong reference photo**: Front-facing, well-lit, high-res (min 1024×1024), minimal filters\n2. **High-resolution references**: Even lighting, clear facial detail\n3. **Explicit instructions**: \"Use the supplied image as reference for the person's appearance\"\n4. **Iterative refinement**: If features drift after many edits, restart conversation with detailed description\n\n#### Limitations\nSmall changes in lighting, styling, background, camera angle, or prompt wording can cause reinterpretation of:\n- Eye shape\n- Jawline  \n- Skin texture\n- Overall facial proportions\n\n#### Virtual Try-On Template\n```\nCreate a professional e-commerce fashion photo. Using the reference image of [person description], show them wearing [clothing item from second image]. Generate a realistic, full-body shot in [environment]. Ensure lighting and shadows match the environment. Preserve the person's facial features, skin tone, and hair exactly as shown in the reference image. [Aspect ratio].\n```\n\n#### Real-World Example (from Google docs)\n```\nCreate a professional e-commerce fashion photo. Take the blue floral dress from the first image and let the woman from the second image wear it. Generate a realistic, full-body shot of the woman wearing the dress, with the lighting and shadows adjusted to match an outdoor environment.\n```\n\n### Multi-Image Fusion for Fashion\n- Combine product shots with models\n- Merge clothing items from different images\n- Transfer style/aesthetic between images\n- Template: \"Take [element from image 1] and place it with/on [element from image 2]\"\n\n---\n\n## 4. System Prompts & Few-Shot Examples\n\n### Few-Shot Support\n**YES** - Gemini supports and benefits from few-shot examples for image generation.\n\n#### Best Practices\n1. **Always include few-shot examples** - prompts without them are \"likely to be less effective\"\n2. **Show format and style**: Provide 1-3 example image-text pairs demonstrating desired output\n3. **Consistent formatting**: Pay attention to XML tags, whitespace, newlines, example splitters\n4. **Use prefixes**: Add labels like \"Input:\", \"Output:\", \"The result is:\" for easier parsing\n\n#### Example Structure\n```\nHere are examples of the style I want:\n\nExample 1:\nInput: \"minimalist white sneaker on concrete\"\n[reference image]\n\nExample 2:  \nInput: \"vintage leather boot on wood surface\"\n[reference image]\n\nNow create:\nInput: \"black ankle boot on marble surface\"\n```\n\n#### Gemini Ultra Specifics\nCan take few-shot prompts with interleaved image-text where user provides information about colors and image suggestions. The model identifies patterns and applies relationships to new examples.\n\n---\n\n## 5. Limitations & Workarounds\n\n### Known Limitations (as of Feb 2026)\n\n#### 1. Complex Typography\n**Issue**: Generating complex typography or perfect text rendering on first attempt requires iteration\n**Workaround**: \n- Use conversational refinement\n- Be extremely explicit about font, size, placement\n- Follow up with: \"Make the text larger\" or \"Move the text to the left\"\n\n#### 2. Character Consistency Drift\n**Issue**: Features can drift across many iterative edits, especially eye shape, jawline, skin texture\n**Workaround**:\n- Restart conversation with detailed character description\n- Use high-res reference images (1024×1024+)\n- Include explicit instruction to preserve specific features\n- Avoid excessive iterative edits in single conversation\n\n#### 3. Aspect Ratio Control\n**Issue**: Model may not preserve input image aspect ratio during editing\n**Workaround**:\n- Be explicit: \"Update the input image... Do not change the input aspect ratio\"\n- If multiple images uploaded, model adopts aspect ratio of LAST image\n- For new images: provide reference image with correct dimensions\n\n#### 4. Safety Filter Over-Sensitivity\n**Issue**: Overly cautious filters rejecting innocuous prompts\n**Workaround**:\n- Use hyper-specific, detailed descriptions\n- Add artistic/commercial context explicitly\n- Reframe negative constraints as positive descriptions\n- Configure safety thresholds via API\n\n#### 5. Image Format\n**Issue**: Gemini 2.5 Flash generates JPEG instead of PNG/WEBP\n**Workaround**: Accept JPEG output or use post-processing to convert\n\n### General Workarounds\n\n#### Iteration Strategy\n- Don't expect perfection on first try\n- Use conversational refinement: \"That's great, but can you make the lighting warmer?\"\n- Make small, incremental changes rather than complete redesigns\n\n#### Camera Control\nUse cinematic/photographic language:\n- `wide-angle shot`, `macro shot`, `low-angle perspective`\n- `85mm portrait lens`, `Dutch angle`  \n- `bokeh`, `depth of field`, `shallow focus`\n\n---\n\n## 6. Negative Prompts vs. Gemini's Approach\n\n### Diffusion Models (Stable Diffusion)\n- Have dedicated \"negative prompt\" parameters\n- Work through mutual cancellation in latent space\n- **Limitation**: Delayed effect - negative prompts only work AFTER positive prompts render content\n- Introducing negative in early diffusion stages paradoxically generates the specified object\n\n### Gemini's Approach: Semantic Positive Reframing\n**No traditional negative prompt support** - instead, use \"semantic negative prompts\":\n\n#### Instead of:\n❌ \"no cars, no people, no buildings\"\n\n#### Use:\n✅ \"an empty, deserted street with no signs of traffic, showing only the road surface and sky\"\n\n#### Why This Works\n- Pure affirmative framing is most reliable\n- Gemini's language understanding excels at positive scene description\n- Avoids the \"negation problem\" inherent in diffusion models\n\n#### Template\n```\nInstead of saying what NOT to include, describe the desired scene positively:\n- \"no clutter\" → \"clean, minimal composition with empty space\"\n- \"no text\" → \"image without any lettering or typography\"  \n- \"no people\" → \"isolated product shot on plain background\"\n```\n\n---\n\n## 7. Fashion-Specific Use Cases & Benchmarks\n\n### Image Quality (Benchmarks)\n\n#### Photorealism\n- **State-of-the-art (SOTA) photorealism**\n- Lower Fréchet Inception Distance (FID) score than competitors\n- Users confirm superior output vs. top models with \"beautiful depth of field, realistic shading, intricate detail\"\n\n#### Fashion Product Performance\n- Excels at e-commerce product photography\n- Generates photorealistic scenes reducing need for physical photoshoots\n- Strong adherence to visual templates (consistent product catalog generation)\n\n### Real-World Fashion Applications\n\n#### 1. Product Photography\n```\nA high-resolution, studio-lit product photograph of a minimalist ceramic coffee mug in matte black, presented on a polished concrete surface. The lighting is a three-point softbox setup designed to create soft, diffused highlights and eliminate harsh shadows. The camera angle is a slightly elevated 45-degree shot to showcase its clean lines. Ultra-realistic, with sharp focus on the steam rising from the coffee. Square image.\n```\n\n#### 2. Flat-Lay Composition\n- Creates top-down \"flat lay\" photographs\n- Places products alongside included items on specified surfaces\n- Uses master image as foundation to match lighting, colors, textures\n\n#### 3. E-commerce Fashion Photos\nExample from Google: Take dress from Image 1 + model from Image 2 → generate realistic full-body shot with adjusted lighting/shadows in outdoor environment\n\n#### 4. Virtual Try-On\n- Upload selfie → generate full-body digital version\n- Pre-set looks: Casual, Formal, Summer Dress, Winter Coat\n- Try on clothing AND accessories (shirts, dresses, pants, coats, hats, jewelry, sunglasses)\n- AI accounts for fabric properties, lighting, body shape, posture, perspective\n\n### Comparative Advantages\n- **Multi-image fusion**: Seamless blending for marketing, advertising\n- **Visual template adherence**: Uniform product mockups for entire catalog\n- **Character consistency**: Same model across multiple product shots\n- **Speed & cost**: $0.039/image, faster than traditional photoshoots\n\n---\n\n## 8. OpenRouter Integration\n\n### API Endpoint\n`POST /api/v1/chat/completions`\n\n### Required Parameters\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"google/gemini-2.5-flash-image-preview\",\n  \"messages\": [\n    {\n      \"role\": \"user\",\n      \"content\": \"Generate a beautiful sunset over mountains\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"modalities\": [\"image\", \"text\"],\n  \"stream\": false\n}\n```\n\n### Image Configuration Options\n\n#### Aspect Ratio\n```json\n{\n  \"image_config\": {\n    \"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\"\n  }\n}\n```\nSupported: `1:1`, `2:3`, `3:2`, `3:4`, `4:3`, `4:5`, `5:4`, `9:16`, `16:9`, `21:9`\n\n#### Image Size  \n```json\n{\n  \"image_config\": {\n    \"image_size\": \"4K\"\n  }\n}\n```\nSupported: `1K` (default), `2K`, `4K`\n\n#### Combined Example\n```json\n{\n  \"model\": \"google/gemini-3-pro-image-preview\",\n  \"messages\": [...],\n  \"modalities\": [\"image\", \"text\"],\n  \"image_config\": {\n    \"aspect_ratio\": \"16:9\",\n    \"image_size\": \"4K\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n### Response Format\n```json\n{\n  \"choices\": [\n    {\n      \"message\": {\n        \"role\": \"assistant\",\n        \"content\": \"I've generated a beautiful sunset image for you.\",\n        \"images\": [\n          {\n            \"type\": \"image_url\",\n            \"image_url\": {\n              \"url\": \"data:image/png;base64,iVBORw0KGgoAAAANSUhEUgAA...\"\n            }\n          }\n        ]\n      }\n    }\n  ]\n}\n```\n\n**Format**: Base64-encoded data URLs (typically PNG)\n\n### Streaming Support\n```json\n{\n  \"stream\": true\n}\n```\nImages arrive in delta chunks within streaming response.\n\n---\n\n## 9. Production Readiness & Latest Updates\n\n### Current Status (Feb 2026)\n- **General Availability**: February 3, 2026 - ready for production\n- **Preview Status**: Still in preview, expect rapid updates\n- **10 Aspect Ratios**: Supports all major content formats (cinematic landscapes → vertical social media)\n\n### Model Options\n1. **Gemini 2.5 Flash Image** (Nano Banana)\n   - Standard: 1024px\n   - $30/1M output tokens\n   - OpenRouter: `google/gemini-2.5-flash-image-preview`\n\n2. **Gemini 3 Pro Image** (preview)\n   - Up to 4096px resolution\n   - Higher quality, slower generation\n   - Supports generating images of people with updated safety filters\n\n### Retirement Notice\n⚠️ **Important**: Gemini 2.0 Flash and Gemini 2.0 Flash-Lite retire **March 31, 2026**. Migrate to `gemini-2.5-flash-lite` or newer.\n\n---\n\n## 10. Key Takeaways for OOTD Fashion Assistant\n\n### Recommended Approach\n\n#### For Flat-Lay Product Photos\n1. Use hyper-specific prompts with photographic language\n2. Specify overhead perspective, surface material, lighting setup\n3. Request square 1:1 or product-friendly aspect ratios (3:4, 4:5)\n4. Mention \"e-commerce product photography\" for safety context\n\n#### For Virtual Try-On\n1. Use character consistency with reference images (min 1024×1024)\n2. Explicitly instruct to preserve facial features\n3. Expect some variation - use iterative refinement\n4. Consider using Gemini 3 Pro Image for higher quality at scale\n\n#### For Content Policy Compliance\n1. Always include \"product photography\", \"e-commerce\", \"fashion editorial\" context\n2. Be hyper-specific about materials, colors, styles\n3. Use \"fictional model\" or \"character\" language for human figures\n4. Configure safety thresholds via API if rejections occur\n\n#### For Multi-Product Scenes\n1. Leverage multi-image fusion (up to 5 images)\n2. Use master image to establish lighting/color palette\n3. Generate consistent catalog shots from single template\n4. Cost-effective vs. traditional photoshoots ($0.039/image)\n\n### Technical Integration\n- Use OpenRouter API with `modalities: [\"image\", \"text\"]`\n- Always specify aspect ratio for consistency\n- Store base64 images or convert to permanent URLs\n- Implement retry logic for safety filter rejections (with positive reframing)\n- Use streaming for better UX during generation\n\n---\n\n## Sources\n\n### Official Documentation\n- [Introducing Gemini 2.5 Flash Image](https://developers.googleblog.com/introducing-gemini-2-5-flash-image/)\n- [Gemini 2.5 Flash Image Documentation](https://docs.cloud.google.com/vertex-ai/generative-ai/docs/models/gemini/2-5-flash-image)\n- [Nano Banana Image Generation](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/image-generation)\n- [How to Prompt Gemini 2.5 Flash Image](https://developers.googleblog.com/en/how-to-prompt-gemini-2-5-flash-image-generation-for-the-best-results/)\n- [Gemini Models Overview](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/models)\n\n### Best Practices & Guides\n- [Prompting Tips for Image Generation](https://blog.google/products-and-platforms/products/gemini/image-generation-prompting-tips/)\n- [Prompt Design Strategies](https://ai.google.dev/gemini-api/docs/prompting-strategies)\n- [Getting Started with Gemini](https://www.promptingguide.ai/models/gemini)\n- [Gemini Image Prompting Handbook](https://github.com/pauhu/gemini-image-prompting-handbook)\n\n### Technical Analysis\n- [10 Steps for Product AI Generation](https://www.philschmid.de/gemini-image-generation-product)\n- [Nano Banana Prompt Engineering](https://minimaxir.com/2025/11/nano-banana-prompts/)\n- [Character Consistency Guide](https://aifacefy.com/blog/detail/How-to-Generate-Consistent-Characters-with-Nano-Banana-Gemini-2-5-Flash-f04e03416688/)\n- [Generating Consistent Imagery](https://towardsdatascience.com/generating-consistent-imagery-with-gemini/)\n\n### OpenRouter Integration\n- [OpenRouter Image Generation Docs](https://openrouter.ai/docs/guides/overview/multimodal/image-generation)\n- [Gemini 2.5 Flash Image on OpenRouter](https://openrouter.ai/google/gemini-2.5-flash-image-preview)\n\n### Benchmarks & Comparisons\n- [Gemini Image Analysis](https://gregrobison.medium.com/from-hype-to-workflow-an-in-depth-analysis-of-googles-gemini-2-5-9c02aceb3f0a)\n- [AI Image Generation 2025: DALL-E vs Gemini vs Stable Diffusion](https://www.weblineindia.com/blog/ai-image-generation-dalle-vs-gemini-vs-stable-diffusion/)\n\n### Virtual Try-On & Fashion\n- [Google Virtual Try-On Tool](https://petapixel.com/2025/12/15/googles-virtual-try-on-tool-lets-you-visualize-yourself-in-any-outfit-from-just-a-selfie/)\n- [Virtual Try-On with RCS](https://developer.vonage.com/en/blog/virtually-try-clothes-on-with-gemini-nano-banana-via-rcs)\n\n### Safety & Content Policy\n- [Safety Evaluation Study](https://www.preprints.org/manuscript/202511.0211)\n- [Content Policy Issues](https://github.com/google-gemini/cookbook/issues/568)\n- [Gemini Safety Guidelines](https://gemini.google/policy-guidelines/)\n- [Troubleshooting Guide](https://www.aifreeapi.com/en/posts/nano-banana-pro-image-generation-refused)"
